  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Lincoln Bishop University, formerly known as Bishop Grosseteste University until 2025, is a public university located in the city of Lincoln, England. It was founded as a teacher training college and is currently a public university.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>With a focus on personalised learning, the university provides small class sizes, allowing for close interactions between you and lecturers. Plus, you’ll have access to a variety of extracurricular activities, from clubs and societies to volunteering opportunities.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>The university offers a range of campus-managed housing. These include the Student Village, Wickham Hall, and Constance Stewart Hall, which are en-suite flats with shared kitchen/living areas.</p><p style=\"text-align:center;\"><i>If you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to </i><a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\"><i>download our app</i></a><i> and check out the Stays feature!</i></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p>acilities<br><strong>Library</strong><br>The university offers a modern, well-equipped library with a wide range of online journals, e-books, and academic databases.</p><p><strong>Sports</strong><br>The university offers various sports clubs through its Students' Union, including popular options like men's football, rugby, badminton, and netball.</p><p><strong>Laboratory</strong><br>On campus, you’ll find several specialised, state-of-the-art facilities, including an Archaeology Lab, a Human Performance Laboratory, a dedicated Business Hub, and more.</p><p><strong>Cafeteria</strong><br>You can find a variety of dining options on campus for fresh food and beverages.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
